[agent] ## Result
[agent] **Diverging feature: `f2`**
[agent] ### How I found it (all work on the platform)
[agent] 1. Registered two feature groups via the `hops` CLI — `skew_train` (300 rows from `training_sample.csv`) and `skew_serve` (200 rows from `serving_log.csv`) — and inserted the CSVs.
[agent] 2. Joined them on `entity_id` in the offline store via `hops sql` (Trino, `delta` catalog) and computed per-feature mean absolute difference across the 200 shared entities:
[agent] | feature | mean abs diff (train vs serve) |
[agent] |---|---|
[agent] | f1 | 0.0 |
[agent] | **f2** | **7.73** |
[agent] | f3 | 0.0 |
[agent] | f4 | 0.0 |
