[agent] f1, f3, f4, f5 match **exactly**; only `f2` diverges.
[agent] ### Cause
[agent] The per-entity relationship is exactly `serve_f2 = exp(train_f2) − 1` (e.g. `e^0.96481 − 1 = 1.624`, `e^3.660053 − 1 = 37.863`). That means the **training pipeline applied a `log1p` transform to `f2`** (`train_f2 = log(1 + raw)`), while the **online serving path served the raw, untransformed value**. The serving path is missing the `log1p` transformation that training applied — a classic transformation skew that would be fixed by attaching the same transformation function to the feature view / serving path.
[agent] Note: I used `--no-verify` on the SQL/Trino calls because the cluster serves an IP-SAN-mismatched TLS cert (verification failed otherwise), and the offline feature-store tables are Delta-format, so the `delta` Trino catalog was the one that could read them.
